    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="2.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:WiLad">Wl lad</ref> 2.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="484" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gif se Fræncisca byð ofercuman, he gyfe þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> cynge III pund.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="484" ed="#liebermann"/>Si Francigena uictus fuerit, persoluat regi LX sol.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#WiLad_2-2.lnote.oe.2"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="2.2" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="232" ed="#robertson"/>7 gif se Fræncisca byð ofercuman, he gyfe þam cynge III pund.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="484" ed="#liebermann"/>2, 2. Und wenn der Französische<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#WiLad_2-2.lnote.de.1"/> [Kläger] überwunden worden ist, zahle er dem König 3<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#WiLad_2-2.lnote.de.2"/> Pfund [= 60 Schill. <hi rend="italic">Quadr</hi>.].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">2, 2. And if the French [plaintiff] has been overcome, he shall pay the king 3 pounds [= 60 shill. <hi rend="italic">Quadr</hi>.].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="233" ed="#robertson"/>And if the Frenchman is defeated, he shall give the king £3.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="484"><ref target="clause:WlArt_6-2">Wl art 6.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">6, 2</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:WlArt_6-2">Wl art 6.2</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 232–233 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 484, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="WiLad_2-2.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">484</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Sc K Hg</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">missing in Sc K Hg</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="WiLad_2-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">273</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Falsche Klage (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 7; Verleumdung 3) des Engländers wird nach Angelsächsischem Rechte gestraft und daher nicht erwähnt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">False accusation (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 7; Verleumdung 3) by the Englishman is punished under Anglo-Saxon law and is therefore not mentioned</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="WiLad_2-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">273</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Zweikampf 17b; Königsbann 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Zweikampf 17b; Königsbann 1</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
